title: 'M1.6 slice 2 reading: the launch-token theft card has no effect'
summary: 'The spec says theft raises a fresh-presence gate-class card naming the revoked connection but not what allow/deny do. Reading: the revocation already happened and stands either way; allow records ''that was me'', deny ''that was not me''; neither restores the session, so no decision can widen access. No timeout (B6: silence decides nothing). One card per revoked connId. Raised from #socket dispatch after the socket.auth.theft row, so web/* is untouched.'
